+### `parseDataURL(input)`
+
+Parses a `data:` URL into `{ mimeType, base64, data }`. `base64` is a boolean, `mimeType` defaults to `text/plain`, and `data` is the raw (not decoded) payload. Throws a `TypeError` for invalid input.
+
+**Example:**
+
+```js
+parseDataURL("data:text/plain;base64,SGVsbG8=");
+// { mimeType: "text/plain", base64: true, data: "SGVsbG8=" }
+```
+
